title start
name: title-plan-database-server
kind: plan
tags: ecosystem server database
Plan: database server, CLI door and web door
title end

chapter start
name: section-goal
title start
name: title-goal
Goal
title end
paragraph start
name: paragraph-the-notation-database
The notation database is served by the ecosystem server, so the
editor, shell, multiplexer and a local mind map website read one
index. CLI packages use the Unix socket. The website uses HTTP and
WebSocket on 127.0.0.1. Both doors call the same handle function.
contract start
id: q575f3b
question: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
contract end
answer start
for: q575f3b
asked: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
Yes. One outcome: one index served to every package and the website.

answer end
paragraph end
paragraph start
name: paragraph-decided-by-shape
Decided by Shape: Unix socket stays for the CLI. HTTP plus
WebSocket for the web. WebAssembly for the website. Plan approved
on 2026-11-17. Build in step order. When a step is finished and
he confirms on screen, delete it from this plan and update
AIU NOTATION/README.aiu in the same script. Any AI continues at
the first step left.
contract start
id: q575f3b
question: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
contract end
answer start
for: q575f3b
asked: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
No. It records decisions and rules, not the goal.
answer end
paragraph end
paragraph start
name: paragraph-decided-order
Decided. The mind map is the last thing built. First the
server and the website exchange commands (read, write, delete,
move) through a wasm bridge. The bridge has no interface at all,
not even a basic one.
contract start
id: q575f3b
question: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
contract end
answer start
for: q575f3b
asked: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
No. It records a decision, not the goal.
answer end
paragraph end
paragraph start
name: paragraph-decided-mindmap
Decided. Mind map rules: real boxes with titles, boxes inside
boxes, never dots. Shape builds the structure by hand. Every new
branch has a master file. Layout and direction of each file are
written in the files themselves. Nothing auto arranges.
contract start
id: q575f3b
question: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
contract end
answer start
for: q575f3b
asked: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
No. It records a decision, not the goal.
answer end
paragraph end
paragraph start
name: paragraph-decided-no-reject
Decided. The server never rejects a write. It reports errors
and holds a list of them.
contract start
id: q575f3b
question: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
contract end
answer start
for: q575f3b
asked: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
No. It records a decision, not the goal.
answer end
paragraph end
paragraph start
name: paragraph-decided-git
Decided. Git is always on, local only: no remote, no push. The
server uses the repo it finds by walking up from the file to the
nearest .git, whatever the layout. Every save, delete, move and
overwrite is its own commit, however many. Shape deletes old
commits himself. With no .git found the server reports an error
and never blocks.
contract start
id: q575f3b
question: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
contract end
answer start
for: q575f3b
asked: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
No. It records a decision, not the goal.
answer end
paragraph end
paragraph start
name: paragraph-decided-handshake
Decided. SHA-1 and base64 for the WebSocket handshake are
written by hand in the server. Crates are used only when the work
is too big to write or not worth writing.
contract start
id: q575f3b
question: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
contract end
answer start
for: q575f3b
asked: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
No. It records a decision, not the goal.
answer end
paragraph end
paragraph start
name: paragraph-decided-crate-path
Decided. The server uses the notation crate by path, as the
editor does. It does not run the notation binary per request.
contract start
id: q575f3b
question: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
contract end
answer start
for: q575f3b
asked: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
No. It records a decision, not the goal.
answer end
paragraph end
paragraph start
name: paragraph-decided-port-site
Decided. Port 8080, read from AIU_SERVER_PORT, bound to 127.0.0.1.
Tailscale comes later and only changes the bind address. The
website lives in its own folder AIU ECOSYSTEM/website, next to
server, never inside it. The server only serves files from it.
contract start
id: q575f3b
question: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
contract end
answer start
for: q575f3b
asked: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
No. It records a decision, not the goal.
answer end
paragraph end
paragraph start
name: paragraph-decided-index
Decided. The server indexes the folder given to load FOLDER. It
reindexes a file right after a write through the server and on
the reload command. It does not watch the disk.
contract start
id: q575f3b
question: Can the goal be stated as one outcome, not an activity?
